============================================================
  HUMAN FINDINGS GATE
============================================================

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The bug causing inflated total_output_tokens under KV-cache preemption was confirmed and the fix fully eliminates it. With preemptions enabled (--total-kv-blocks 600), total_output_tokens dropped from 114,630 (before fix) to 105,082 (after fix), exactly matching the preemption-free control run. The fix has zero side effects when no preemptions occur.

  * H-main CONFIRMED: The double-counting bug inflated total_output_tokens by 9,548 tokens (+9.09%) when 265 preemptions occurred. After patching sim/batch_formation.go and sim/simulator.go to track DecodedTokens on PreemptedRequest and subtract them during rescheduling, the metric exactly matches the no-preemption baseline (105,082).
  * H-control-negative CONFIRMED: With a large KV cache (60,000 blocks, 0 preemptions), total_output_tokens is identical before and after the fix (105,082), confirming the patch is narrowly scoped to the preemption path only.
  * All existing tests pass and a new regression test (TestPreemption_TotalOutputTokens_NoDoubleCount) validates the fix. The experiment is valid with no surprises or discrepancies — both arms matched predictions exactly.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

